<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The BASIC provider set, and "basic" is the membership RULE rather than a position in a list (D144):
    everything that reaches a model needing nothing beyond Lyntai.Core and the BCL — the spawned CLIs
    (`claude`, `codex`), any OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint (OpenAI, Ollama, OpenRouter, Azure) for chat
    AND embeddings, and the in-process model2vec embedder. One package because their dependency footprint
    is the same (no native payload), so bundling costs a consumer nothing.

    Packages stay SEPARATE when they drag something a consumer may not want: Lyntai.Providers.LlamaSharp
    (LLamaSharp + a native backend), Lyntai.Storage.Sqlite (a native SQLite binary),
    Lyntai.Tools.Mcp (ModelContextProtocol.Core), Lyntai.Secrets.Dpapi (Windows-only).
    See docs/DECISIONS.md D25.

    The 2.0.1 MERGE changed no namespace, deliberately — a consumer edits one PackageReference and no
    `using`. The HTTP family was renamed later and for its own reason (Lyntai.Providers.Http, D135), so the
    namespaces here are .ClaudeCli / .CodexCli / .Http, plus Lyntai.Embeddings.Model2Vec (D121).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Lyntai.Providers.Basic</PackageId>
    <Description>The Lyntai LLM backends that need nothing beyond Lyntai.Core and the BCL: the authenticated `claude` and `codex` CLIs, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenAI/Ollama/OpenRouter/Azure) for chat + embeddings, and an in-process model2vec embedder — bundled because none of them ships a native payload. Media backends live in Lyntai.Generation; local GGUF inference is Lyntai.Providers.LlamaSharp.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Lyntai.Core\Lyntai.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" />
    <!-- The only third-party reference here, and it must stay the only one: this package's whole membership
         rule is Core + the BCL, so anything added below moves a backend out of it. On the
         Microsoft.Extensions.* band D26 allows; the HTTP backend needs a named-client factory. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Lyntai.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
